0073: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
0074:     """
0075:     Compress the stacked colored bars into a compact ordered table with the control pixel on the selected row.
0076: 
0077:     Input structure
0078:     - A background grid contains several full-width colored bars from top to
0079:       bottom; the last bar is the base/separator color.
0080:     - Each non-base bar may have an aligned three-column comb motif below it,
0081:       alternating side-pair rows with solid rows.
0082:     - A singleton control pixel sits away from the colored motifs.
0083: 
0084:     Rule
0085:     - Make one output row per non-base bar, preserving top-to-bottom order.
0086:     - In that row, paint the bar color once for each solid three-pixel row in
0087:       its motif, then paint the base-bar color in the separator column.
0088:     - The singleton control pixel sits immediately above the base bar. Among
0089:       motifs whose open side-pair parity is compatible with that bottom row,
0090:       put the control pixel in the output row with the fewest solid rows; use
0091:       horizontal distance to the motif center only to break count ties.
0092: 
0093:     Key insight
0094:     - The vertical comb height is a count, while the control pixel is read by
0095:       projecting it onto the center gap of compatible comb rows rather than by
0096:       its vertical band alone.
0097:     """
0098:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
0099:     bg = get_bg(g)
0100:     bars = _full_width_bars(g, bg)
